/** @page openldapreleasenotes Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @anchor openldap_rel13
    @section openldap_rel20 openldap Module 2.0

    @subsection openldap_rel20_overview Overview

    Version 2.0 adds transaction support, enterprise authentication, and helper modules for pooling,
    asynchronous operations, directory administration, and LDIF import/export. It includes all changes
    previously planned for the unreleased 1.3 version. See @ref openldaphelpermodules for examples.

    @subsection openldap_rel20_features New Features

    - LDAP transactions (RFC 5805) through @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::txnStart() "LdapClient::txnStart()" and
      @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::txnEnd() "LdapClient::txnEnd()", with automatic rollback through @ref LdapTransaction
    - SASL authentication through @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::saslBind() "LdapClient::saslBind()", including GSSAPI,
      DIGEST-MD5, EXTERNAL, and SCRAM; channel binding, security properties, security strength limits, and
      canonicalization controls are described in @ref openldapsaslguide
    - @ref ldapconnectionpoolintro "LdapConnectionPool" provides thread-safe connection pooling, health checks,
      reconnection, and configurable retries through @ref LdapConnectionPool::withConnectionRetry()
    - @ref ldaphelperintro "LdapHelper" provides @ref LdapEntry, @ref LdapSearchIterator, @ref LdapDn, and
      @ref LdapClientHelper; health checks and identity queries use @ref LdapClientHelper::ping() and
      @ref LdapClientHelper::whoAmI()
    - @ref ldapasyncintro "LdapAsync" provides @ref LdapFuture and @ref LdapAsyncClient for parallel LDAP operations
    - @ref ldifhelperintro "LdifHelper" provides @ref LdifReader and @ref LdifWriter for LDIF (RFC 2849) import/export
    - @ref ldapactivedirectoryintro "LdapActiveDirectory" provides @ref ActiveDirectoryClient for paged searches,
      range retrieval, GUID/SID decoding, and searches for deleted objects
    - Server and client controls on LDAP operations; see @ref ldap_control_constants for control OIDs
    - Paged searches (RFC 2696) through the \c page-size option of @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::search() "LdapClient::search()",
      allowing searches beyond Active Directory's default 1000-entry limit
    - Binary attributes through the \c binary-attributes and \c all-binary search options, with automatic handling
      of known binary attributes; see @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::search() "LdapClient::search()"
    - Generic extended operations through @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::extendedOp() "LdapClient::extendedOp()";
      see @ref ldap_extop_constants for common operation OIDs
    - RFC 4514 DN parsing with escaped characters and multi-valued RDNs through @ref LdapDn, including
      @ref LdapDn::escape() and @ref LdapDn::unescape(); @ref LdapUrl parses RFC 4516 LDAP URLs and
      @ref LdapSchema exposes directory schema information
    - Interruptible I/O allows sandboxed programs to terminate gracefully before LDAP operations
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5116">issue 5116</a>)

    @subsection openldap_rel20_fixes Bug Fixes

    - Fixed a crash when passing multi-valued attributes to @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::add() "LdapClient::add()" or
      @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::modify() "LdapClient::modify()"
    - Fixed @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::copy() "LdapClient::copy()" failing to authenticate the copied connection
      because successful bind parameters were not retained
    - Fixed unreachable code in @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::del() "LdapClient::del()"
    - Corrected return types for @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::compare() "LdapClient::compare()" and
      @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::isSecure() "LdapClient::isSecure()"
    - Prevented a null distinguished name returned by the LDAP library from causing a crash in
      @ref OpenLdap::LdapClient::search() "LdapClient::search()"

